:"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation 2: corrected the `_recheck_drift` attribution to the apply loop before `_apply_one`, added a worked inert-vs-real-payload example, and made the rev-parse count AC explicit (count equals emitted mutations; 0 in the converged case).","timestamp":1788871285892742001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation 3: replaced the vague `_mutation_to_batch_dict` survival wording with the exact inline predicate implemented in differ.py: retain only Jira update fields whose resolved value differs from Jira, and skip emit when none remain. The examples now cover both empty-local reachable clears and metadata-only inert drift.","timestamp":1788872282030400001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation 4: widened the explicitly Jira-reachable survival set to include `parent` and `reporter`, which are dispatched by dedicated update sub-calls before scalar allowlist filtering. Added parent/reporter negative-control coverage to ensure real routed writes are not suppressed.","timestamp":1788873165178242001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan update after applying advisory: extracted the Jira-reachable update field set into `_field_contract.py`, reused it from `dispatch_apply_phases.py`, and widened file impact accordingly so the differ and dispatch path cannot silently drift.","timestamp":1788875857385219001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation refinement: preserved the canonical compute_mutations local-vs-Jira contract by making Jira-unreachable suppression explicit opt-in for the snapshot-key-set run_differs caller. Full affected conflict/differ suites now pass after the prior full verify exposed the over-broad default behavior.","timestamp":1788881382400949001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan update after full-suite failure: narrowed the fix to the actual key-set prev marker. The snapshot caller opts into skipping branch-3 updates when the prev-side entry is `{}`; default compute_mutations behavior remains unchanged for true local-vs-Jira callers. Affected conflict/differ suites pass.","timestamp":1788882678975635001}],"created_at":1788158735491395001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[],"description":"With a key-set prev, keys present in both prev and curr route to `_compute_mutations_emit_both`\nwith an empty `local_fields`, producing ~516 mutations per pass that are provably inert but not free.\nSkip them. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Why\nEach inert mutation still drives one per-mutation loop iteration in the batch apply path\n(`applier.py:639-640`), which calls `_recheck_drift` ->\n`concurrency.snapshot_head(repo_root)` — **a `git rev-parse` subprocess** — before dispatching via `_apply_one`. So ~516 extra\ngit invocations per pass, ~516 `RECON: batch_outcome` stderr lines, ~516 outcome records in the\nmanifest, and an inflated `mutation_count` so a converged pass reports 516 instead of 0. It also\nenlarges the HEAD-drift window. Under `BOOTSTRAP_STRICT` (cap 10) or `BOOTSTRAP_THROTTLE` (cap 100)\nthese compete for cap slots with genuine work (`apply_planning.py:90-101`) and can starve it —\nproduction defaults to `LIVE` (cap `None`), so that risk is latent, not live.\n\n## Approach\nTreat the empty dict written by the key-set prev snapshot as a snapshot-route marker, not as a\ncanonical local ticket with every Jira field cleared. Add an explicit opt-in flag to\n`compute_mutations` for the snapshot-key-set caller in `run_differs.py`; when that flag is set,\n`_compute_mutations_emit_both` skips branch-3 update emission for keys whose local-side value is\nempty. The default `compute_mutations(local_state, jira_state)` behavior remains unchanged for\ncanonical local-vs-Jira callers, including genuine empty-local clear/update semantics.\n\nConcrete examples: with the opt-in set, key-set prev `{\"PROJ-1\": {}}` plus current Jira fields\nemits no branch-3 update, so no inert mutation enters the pass tally/apply path. Without the opt-in,\nthe same pair still emits the existing canonical clear/update. Parent-only and reporter-only changes\nalso remain emitted in the default canonical path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With a key-set prev over a real corpus, `(outbound, update)` mutations with an empty effective\n      payload are **0** (down from ~516). Tier: **unit** on `compute_mutations` + the corpus script.\n- [ ] Mutations with a genuine non-empty effective payload are still emitted unchanged, including\n      parent-only and reporter-only branch-3 changes that route through dedicated outbound sub-calls\n      before scalar filtering — the negative controls. Tier: **unit**.\n- [ ] `mutation_count` on a converged pass is 0. Tier: **integration** asserting the pass record.\n- [ ] `git rev-parse` invocation count per pass equals the number of actually emitted mutations (0 on\n      the converged-pass case in AC3). Tier: **integration** with a counting shim.\n\n## Files\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_field_contract.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py`, tests\n\nScope: S. Depends on A4-2.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py","reason":"add opt-in branch-3 suppression for empty key-set prev markers while preserving default differ semantics"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py","reason":"opt the snapshot-key-set differ caller into empty-marker branch-3 suppression"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","95da-0b4f-06a8-4b9c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"95da-0b4f-06a8-4b9c","parent_status_uuid":"da77eeeb-bbf1-40f6-b547-ae7a057ac4f2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"02aa-d30e-828a-4f21","ticket_type":"task","title":"A4-3: skip the differ's branch-3 emit when the resolved payload cannot reach Jira","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b9c98242-900d-49fc-8a2d-15c012daa569","73b481e2-1d60-40d4-bf2a-6035aa4b3392","b9bfe275-3377-4d46-a1de-0fbcd1b68efa","b363e53b-13ec-4f8c-b5e6-6bfe4f292281","d2e2e62a-9812-4535-9023-31a2f8efaaef","aab64951-dadb-43df-9a65-380614d41cbb","0a762fcf-5c15-4ec6-9638-f4f499efa45e","bb7f3922-48d4-4e8f-8ebb-840484ab4dab","70047d11-5d9f-42be-9229-a6fcc724268c","da77eeeb-bbf1-40f6-b547-ae7a057ac4f2","2201f4df-7ecb-43d0-997b-a58e82299c19","57b47e59-45d6-4bf5-8357-909aae157c9d","52a78cbb-1830-4650-9f24-d20365e6e18d","9bdc91fd-0191-4be3-8770-401d8e91f5f8","08c43445-fdf8-4eef-9aaf-fd67d726a224","06deb4bd-d8c7-476d-88ad-b6a9fc7d09f5","c84f6aca-425e-4223-a1a3-5d6a21d71ad0","63f61903-b999-4a1a-bc9c-f99838c02813","5f5a0f99-63f3-4728-ae3d-0d10d32a17f8","9412e874-29d5-42d6-9c00-9b5ccf8ece8b","69a15bfb-4f0c-4f1d-b9f5-01660625fc00"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788882707746638002,"uuid":"7328e20f-12cf-4866-86c0-218fbfbfafc0"}